{"role":"assistant","content":"Both facts are now pinned down precisely:\n\n1. The `status=$?` assignment is fatal in zsh **regardless of `set -u`** — `status` is a read-only special variable (zsh's alias for `$?`), so line 19 kills the script every single run, before either Telegram branch. The job could never have sent anything, success or failure.\n2. `claude` exits 1 with \"Not logged in\" in the launchd environment — no credentials available to the background job even though the interactive shell is logged in.\n\nNow the fix — rename the variable and add a stderr breadcrumb if the notifier itself fails, so a future silent failure leaves evidence in `nightly-review.err`:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_TSmCgEJNdbtavO7TpZNkLOP8","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"bin/nightly-review.zsh\",\"old_string\":\"cd \\\"$REPO\\\" || { \\\"$NOTIFY\\\" \\\"nightly review: repo missing\\\"; exit 1; }\\n\\nclaude -p \\\"$PROMPT\\\" --output-format text > \\\"$OUT\\\"\\nstatus=$?\\n\\nif [ $status -ne 0 ]; then\\n  \\\"$NOTIFY\\\" \\\"nightly review FAILED (exit $status), see $OUT\\\"\\n  exit $status\\nfi\",\"new_string\":\"cd \\\"$REPO\\\" || { \\\"$NOTIFY\\\" \\\"nightly review: repo missing\\\" || echo \\\"nightly-review: notify.sh failed\\\" >&2; exit 1; }\\n\\nclaude -p \\\"$PROMPT\\\" --output-format text > \\\"$OUT\\\"\\nrc=$?\\n\\nif [ $rc -ne 0 ]; then\\n  \\\"$NOTIFY\\\" \\\"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc), see $OUT\\\" || echo \\\"nightly-review: notify.sh failed\\\" >&2\\n  exit $rc\\nfi\"}"}}]}
